+# Proof outline
+
+1. Preserve the exact finite-field and characteristic hypotheses.
+2. Freeze `A = F[X]`, `K = F⟨X⟩`, the special-linear quotient, and the
+   diagonal action from the source declaration.
+3. Use the rank-four Huang--Shi construction to select one quotient point `z`.
+4. Retain its compact-closure conclusion without weakening the topology.
+5. Retain its nonclosed-orbit conclusion with the exact negation scope.
+6. Introduce the conjunction at that same `z`.
+7. Introduce the existential witness and audit both transport directions.
+
+The detailed hypotheses, inference, output, formal anchor, downstream use,
+exceptional case, and trust boundary for each numbered node occur once in
+`full-study.md`; `proof-units.json` carries the typed DAG.
